Cell["\<\
The four relations of a canonical Lie bialgebra are the defining identities \
of an involutive bi-Lie algebra: the Jacobi identity of the bracket, the \
co-Jacobi identity of the co-bracket, their Drinfeld compatibility, and \
involutivity.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4f9b82e8-c753-4a6f-9ac4-e27e543701cb"],

Cell["\<\
The relations of a canonical Lie bialgebra do not depend on the convention of \
the pairing or on the empty word.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"adb5d2c5-1142-411a-8f0a-e271bde453ff"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The arity ",
 Cell[BoxData["All"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20e3e95e-4dd5-4354-b45f-2bc99eda2fa9"],
 " says that the relation is defined on every positive number of arguments: \
an A-infinity algebra has one relation of each arity, and so has a morphism. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["RelationsQ"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/RelationsQ", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8ef566e3-e325-49eb-bb84-b9073f0ff815"],
 " bounds the arity by the length of the tuples it tests."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a25dac98-b8cb-4332-932c-264e24b1062e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The relations of a cochain complex with a pairing of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b0af8d85-7743-4953-b613-e81cb4cefddf"],
 " are its axioms, each an identity on elements:"
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"73177675-fd4e-4b25-ba41-6fd0d25b4f99"],

